#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Measure|3|2|72|2|passage={{...}} we ſhall haue all the world drinke browne & white '''baſtard'''.}}
# A [[sword]] that is midway in length between a short-sword and a long sword; also [[bastard sword]].
# An inferior quality of soft [[brown sugar]], obtained from [[syrup]]s that have been [[boil]]ed several times.
# A large [[mould]] for [[strain]]ing [[sugar]].
