{{etymid|en|thick end}}
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:butte}}
From {{inh|en|enm|but}}, {{m|enm|butte|t=goal, mark, butt of land}}, from {{inh|en|ang|byt}}, {{m|ang|bytt|t=small piece of land}} and {{m|ang|*butt}} (attested in diminutive {{cog|ang|buttuc|t=end, small piece of land}} > {{cog|en|buttock}}), from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*butt}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*buttaz|t=end, piece}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*bʰudʰnós|gloss=bottom}}, later thematic variant of {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰudʰmḗn|*bʰudʰmḗn ~ *bʰudʰn-}}, perhaps from {{der|en|ine-pro|*dʰewbʰ-|t=deep}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|no|butt|t=stump, block}}, {{cog|fo|buttur|t=wooden block}}, {{cog|is|bútur|t=piece, fragment}}, {{cog|nds|butt|t=blunt, clumsy}}. Influenced by {{cog|fro|but}}, {{m|fro|butte|t=but, mark}}, ultimately from the same {{der|en|gem|-}} source. Compare also {{cog|sq|bythë|t=buttocks}}, {{cog|grc|πυθμήν|t=bottom of vessel}}, {{cog|la|fundus|t=bottom}} and {{cog|sa|बुध्न|tr=budhná|t=bottom}}, from the same {{der|en|ine-pro|-}} root. Related to {{m|en|bottom}}, {{m|en|boot}}. {{PIE word|en|bʰudʰmḗn}}

