##* {{quote-book|en|year=1876|by=Cornelius Tacitus|title=Annals of Tacitus.|author=Alfred John Church and William Jackson Brodribb|page=300
|text=The man was one of the most conspicuously infamous sights in the imperial court, bred, as he had been, in a shoemaker's shop, of a deformed person and vulgar wit, originally introduced as a '''butt'''.}}
## The [[hut]] or shelter of the person who attends to the targets in rifle practice.
