===Etymology===
{{ety|en|:inh|enm:fagot|tree=1}}

From {{inh|en|enm|fagot}}, from {{der|en|fro|fagot|t=bundle of sticks}}, of {{unc|en|nocap=1}} origin. Unlikely from {{cog|pro|fagot}} or {{cog|it|fagotto}}, as these appear later than the Old French term. Compare also {{m+|it|fangotto}} and {{cog|es|fajo|t=bundle, wad}}. Perhaps from a diminutive of {{der|en|la-vul|*facus}}, from {{der|en|grc|φάκελος|t=bundle of wood}}.

The senses relating to persons, though possibly originating as an extension of the sense "bundle of sticks" (compare {{m|en|baggage|baggage}}), may have been reinforced by {{m|en|fag|fag}}, from [[fagging]] and/or by {{m|en|feygele|faygele}}, from {{der|en|yi|פֿייגעלע|t=homosexual|lit=little bird}}, related to {{cog|en|fowl}}.

