===Etymology 5===
Mid 19th century:

* perhaps an abbreviation of {{m|en|scatter}}.
* perhaps representing a {{onomatopoeic|en|title=hiss}} followed by the word {{m|en|cat}}. Compare {{cog|sv|schas|t=shoo, begone}}.<ref>{{R:Lexico}}</ref>
* Alternatively, from the expression {{m|en|quicker than scat||in a great hurry}}, 
* Possibly from {{m|en|scoot}}, from the root of {{m|en|shoot}}. 

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|colloquial}} To leave quickly.
#: {{ux|en|Here comes the principal; we'd better '''scat'''.}}
